From: pocket-debs <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] QWidgetWindow: open the context menu of text input widgets on a touch press and hold
Description:
 Qt widgets get touch input as synthesized mouse events with the left button,
 so the context menu of a QLineEdit, QTextEdit, QPlainTextEdit or of an
 editable combo or spin box could not be opened by touch. With no hardware
 keyboard there was no way to paste text into such a field, nor to copy from
 it: on-screen keyboards have no Ctrl key.
 .
 Send a QContextMenuEvent (reason Mouse) to the widget when a synthesized
 left button press (touch or pen) is held for mousePressAndHoldInterval
 without moving farther than startDragDistance, if the widget or the nearest
 ancestor with Qt::WA_InputMethodEnabled is a text input widget that allows a
 context menu. Widgets in that chain that accept touch events or grab the tap
 and hold gesture are left alone, so applications with their own touch
 handling (item views with kinetic scrolling, Dolphin) keep their behaviour.
 The finger is still down when the menu opens; the release goes to the menu,
 which ignores a release without a press of its own, as after a right button
 press on platforms that open context menus on the press.
 .
 Qt has no press and hold context menu for widgets outside Android (where an
 environment variable enables a right button from a long press), see
 QTBUG-73949 and QTBUG-84179.
Origin: other
Bug: https://bugreports.qt.io/browse/QTBUG-73949
Forwarded: no
License: LGPL-3.0-only OR GPL-2.0-only OR GPL-3.0-only (as the patched file)
Last-Update: 2026-11-24
